st the implementation. That's correct.\n\nI'm second-guessing the testing.T integration design decision in D2—the architecture specifies executing two binaries with identical inputs but doesn't prescribe the API shape. For a testing harness, exposing it as a test helper makes sense, but I should verify this aligns with what the architecture actually requires rather than inventing the interface. I need to track down the correct PRD reference for testutils since it's not explicitly mentioned in the source code, so I'll guide the stitch agent on how to locate it rather than guessing. Now I'm ready to write out the final answer.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":41564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c621281d-5cd7-46c0-a1c6-dec75bb363f5","uuid":"92277d23-9912-4283-80bd-9dcf3381d941"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DjisjA5aVhrL5tzsP8pR1F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (utility implementations), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets).\n\n**Current state**:\n- `pkg/sys/` — source code exists (stat.go, stat_darwin.go, stat_linux.go, terminal.go)\n- `pkg/format/` — source code exists (color.go, size.go, table.go)\n- `pkg/testutils/` — spec complete, no source code on working branch\n- `cmd/version/` — generation target from prd011-magefiles, no source code\n\n**Current release**: rel00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure). Four use cases:\n- uc001-magefiles: excluded by DD7 except cmd/version\n- uc002-format: **already implemented** (source code present)\n- uc003-sys: **already implemented** (source code present)\n- uc004-testutils: **needs implementation** — no source code exists\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\n`pkg/testutils` is the highest-priority remaining work in rel00.0. It is the foundational differential testing harness that every `cmd/` package depends on for verification (P5: libraries before consumers). `pkg/sys/` and `pkg/format/` already have source code and must not be re-proposed. `cmd/version` (the only gen target from uc001-magefiles) depends on infrastructure being in place first.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/testutils DiffTest struct and differential test runner\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find the testutils PRD -- likely prd004-testutils.yaml or prd001-testutils.yaml; read whichever PRD covers pkg/testutils)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/testutils/ component description and DiffTest data structure definition)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc004-testutils.yaml (testutils use case)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (test suite with testutils acceptance criteria)\n      - pkg/sys/terminal.go (existing package pattern -- copyright header, SPDX license, package doc comment referencing PRD, code style)\n      - pkg/format/size.go (existing package pattern for exported function documentation style)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests runner function, binary execution and output comparison, normalization hook support\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define a DiffTest struct with fields for: test name, command-line arguments ([]string), stdin input (string), environment variables ([]string), expected exit code (int), and expected stdout/stderr content -- per the ARCHITECTURE.yaml data structure definition and the testutils PRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement a runner function that accepts a testing.T, a path to the Go binary under test, a path to the reference GNU binary, and a slice of DiffTest cases; for each case, execute both binaries with identical stdin, arguments, and environment, then compare stdout, stderr, and exit code\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"When stdout, stderr, or exit code diverges between the Go binary and the reference binary, fail the test with a report containing: test case name, input arguments, the expected output (from the reference binary), the actual output (from the Go binary), and which stream (stdout/stderr/exit code) diverged\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Support per-case normalization hooks -- functions of type func(string) string -- that are applied to both expected and actual output before comparison, to handle known acceptable differences such as timestamps or absolute paths\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary source file is difftest.go, named after the primary exported type DiffTest -- per project convention (see pkg/sys/terminal.go named after TerminalSize, not sys.go)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"The runner integrates with Go's testing.T so callers in cmd/ packages invoke it from their _test.go files; use t.Helper() so failures report the caller's line number, and t.Run() to create subtests for each DiffTest case\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Follow the copyright header, SPDX-License-Identifier, and package doc comment pattern established in pkg/sys/ and pkg/format/ -- reference the testutils PRD number in the package doc comment\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Use os/exec.Command to run both binaries; capture stdout and stderr into bytes.Buffer; compare exit codes via exec.ExitError; do not import golang.org/x/sys/unix (testutils has no platform-divergent syscall needs)\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"DiffTest struct is exported and defines all fields specified in the testutils PRD and ARCHITECTURE.yaml data structure definition\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"RunDiffTests (or equivalent runner per PRD naming) accepts testing.T, Go binary path, reference binary path, and []DiffTest; runs each case as a t.Run subtest against both binaries\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"When stdout, stderr, or exit code differs between the two binaries, the test failure message includes: case name, input args, expected output, actual output, and the divergent stream\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Normalization hooks are configurable per DiffTest case and are applied to both reference and Go binary output before byte comparison\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/testutils/ succeeds with no compilation errors\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/testutils/ reports no issues\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":41564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c621281d-5cd7-46c0-a1c6-dec75bb363f5","uuid":"bb25176a-b690-4d4e-b10d-4874f2c4de20"}
